id: decisions/022-claim-boundedness
title: "A record that asserts says what it does not claim"
kind: decision-frame
record_shape: header
status: draft
authored_by: agent-on-behalf
authored_via: "Claude Code session on Dave's behalf, 2026-09-12; drafted from the JUDGMENTS.md reversal axis 'claim-boundedness'; recommendation is an attributed inference and ratifies nothing"
version: "1.0.0"
updated: 2026-09-12
template_ref: templates/decision.yawn
principal_ref: principal:dave

axis: claim-boundedness
axis_gloss: "whether a claim states the limits of what it covers, or is asserted without any declared boundary"
poles:
  a: bounded-claim
  b: unbounded-claim
split: lone-exception
draft_status: full
leverage: 12
leverage_formula: "judgments_resolved(25) x split_weight(0.4) x authored_conflict_bonus(1.2)"

question: >
  When a record asserts something that reaches outside the tree — a licence, a
  determinism guarantee, a runtime identity, a research frame — must it also
  carry a boundary naming what must not be assumed, and which kinds of record
  are exempt?

why_it_matters: >
  A claim with no boundary is read by a bot as covering everything, which is how
  a licence line becomes legal advice, a deterministic: true becomes a replay
  guarantee across schema upgrades, and a fluent agent becomes a person; today
  43 of 194 records carry a boundary and nothing says which ones must. Once
  answered, every child Yawn and bot below Dave inherits the habit of writing
  reach beside assertion, so a downstream reader can tell what a record claims
  from what it merely mentions.

state_snapshot:
  description: >
    24 judgments sit at bounded-claim (16 authored) and 1 at unbounded-claim (0
    authored). The repository asserts both directions on this axis.
  attributed_to: TAXONOMY.md
  epistemic_status: observed
  source_refs:
    - JUDGMENTS.md
    - TAXONOMY.md

lacuna:
  kind: unselected_choice
  description: >
    Which kinds Dave regards as claim-bearing; whether a template's placeholder
    boundary: "" counts as present; and whether the twelve must-not-claim items in
    RELATIONSHIP_FIRST section 17 should become the default boundary for every bot
    record.

options:
  - name: A
    description: >
      rule: Every active record carries a top-level `boundary:` block naming what it
      does not claim. A record without one is a draft. Guarantees that hold only
      under conditions (determinism, replay) state the condition under boundary, not
      as a neutral requirements list.
    cost: "151 records lack boundary today; a shrink-only grandfather ledger on the status-vocabulary pattern is needed or the suite goes red for weeks; node indexes and templates would carry boundaries that say nothing."
    risk: "Boundary blocks get pasted mechanically ('this record does not claim anything it does not say'), which is worse than absence because it looks like discipline."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "tests/claim-boundary.test.mjs on the status-vocabulary pattern: every .yawn record outside a by-file grandfather ledger carries a top-level boundary: with at least one non-empty item; the ledger has a ceiling and may only shrink."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0008"
      - "J0150"
      - "J0154"
      - "J0167"
      - "J0168"
      - "J0138"
  - name: B
    description: >
      rule: A record may assert without a boundary. boundary: stays optional; a
      reader infers the limits of a claim from its kind and context, and absence of
      a boundary is not read as a claim of completeness.
    cost: "Nothing to change; the ownership-and-license record stays as it is. The twelve enumerated must-not-claim items in core/RELATIONSHIP_FIRST_AGENT_ARENA.yawn section 17 become style, not rule."
    risk: "An automation reads references/ownership-and-license.yawn public_use as covering the YAWN name, the domain and the private ledgers; the license audit's own boundary (report risk, never legal advice) has no counterpart on the record it audits."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "None can enforce this; the record would be a line in core/proof-and-boundary.yawn saying boundary: is optional."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0728"
  - name: C
    description: >
      rule: A record whose claims reach outside the tree must carry `boundary:` —
      kinds reference, safety-protocol, automation, contract, receipt, record-log,
      publication, and any record with a license, guarantee, deterministic, identity
      or runtime_status key. carve-out, written down: folder nodes, templates and
      pure indexes may omit boundary because they assert nothing; a record that
      omits it under this exemption is one of those kinds by declaration. A
      conditional guarantee (replay_requires) is restated under boundary as the
      condition under which it fails.
    cost: "Add boundary: to references/ownership-and-license.yawn (MIT covers repository content, not the YAWN name, the yawn.ai domain, private ledgers, or cited third-party works); move core/event-reduction.yawn replay_requires into a boundary line; audit the automation/ and records/ kinds for missing blocks with a shrink-only ledger."
    risk: "The kind list is the enforcement surface, and kind: is itself an open vocabulary (see vocabulary-closure), so a record can dodge the rule by coining a kind."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "tests/claim-boundary.test.mjs: for a named kind list plus a named key list (license, deterministic, guarantee, runtime_status, identity), every matching record carries boundary: with a non-empty item, outside a shrink-only by-file ledger; a second assertion that core/event-reduction.yawn states its replay condition under boundary."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0008"
      - "J0150"
      - "J0167"
      - "J0168"
      - "J0138"
      - "J0728"

recommendation:
  option_ref: C
  confidence: 0.8
  epistemic_status: inferred
  authority: none
  reasoning: >
    Twenty-four judgments sit on the bounded side, sixteen of them authored,
    including the two lists that define the protocol's posture (twelve failure
    modes, twelve things the system must not claim). The single exception is
    REVEALED: references/ownership-and-license.yawn asserts licence, holder and
    public use with no boundary while its two siblings end in six-item boundary
    lists. Nothing in the tree says legal claims are exempt, so the asymmetry is
    an omission, not a preference. A is the honest reading of the authored side
    but would put a boundary on 151 records, most of which assert nothing; C
    scopes the rule to records whose claims reach outside the tree, which is where
    every authored judgment on side A sits. The mechanism already exists for proof
    (validate-proof-refs.mjs covers/not_covered); this extends the same honesty
    from proof scope to claim scope. Not close on direction; only the scope is a
    judgment call.

target_condition:
  mode: decide
  proposed_by: agent-on-behalf
  affected_principals:
    - principal:dave
  ratification_status: proposed
  sufficient_when:
    - "references/ownership-and-license.yawn carries a boundary: block naming what the MIT licence does not cover."
    - "core/event-reduction.yawn states under boundary that determinism holds only while schema version, reducer version, source refs and authority status are unchanged."
    - "A test in tests/ rejects a record of a named kind, or carrying a named claim key, that has no boundary:, and passes with a ledger that may only shrink."

choice:
  selected_by: ""
  option_ref: ""
  authority_ref: ""

proof:
  covers:
    - target_condition
    - options
  falsifier: >
    A new record under references/ or automation/ asserts a licence, a guarantee
    or a runtime identity with no boundary: and npm test stays green; or a
    boundary: block appears whose only item restates the title.
  status: proposed

evidence_sample:
  - "J0008"
  - "J0138"
  - "J0150"
  - "J0154"
  - "J0167"
  - "J0168"
  - "J0728"

boundary:
  - "confidence cannot ratify an objective; this record proposes and Dave decides"
  - "the REVEALED judgments cited here describe what artifacts do, not what Dave chose"

source:
  template: templates/decision.yawn
  axis: TAXONOMY.md
  inventory: JUDGMENTS.md
  id_index: TAXONOMY.md
